# Template for secrets.bndrun, which is deliberately NOT in git (see .gitignore next to this
# file). Copy it, fill in the tokens, and launch.bndrun picks it up through the optional
# `-include: -secrets.bndrun`:
#
#     cp secrets.bndrun.template secrets.bndrun
#
# Everything here arrives as a system property. configs/configuration.json in
# …emf.runtime.config reads each value as $[env:NAME;default=$[prop:NAME;default=…]], so an
# exported environment variable takes precedence over what is set here, and a value left out
# falls back to the default in that file. Nothing in this chain ever puts a credential in git.
# The substitution is done by org.apache.felix.configadmin.plugin.interpolation, wired in
# launch.bndrun via `felix.cm.config.plugins`.
#
# Without this file the runtime starts exactly as before: both MCP servlets come up with an
# empty auth.token, and McpAuthenticationFilter then trusts direct loopback callers only.
#
# WHEN YOU NEED THESE: the filter refuses a request that arrives from loopback *with* an
# X-Forwarded-For / Forwarded header, because that is a local reverse proxy relaying for a
# remote client ("Remote access requires a configured authentication token"). Any tunnel -
# ngrok, cloudflared - in front of the runtime produces exactly that shape, so exposing an
# endpoint and setting its token are one step, not two. A caller then presents the value as
# `Authorization: Bearer <token>`; Anthropic's MCP connector sends the `authorization_token`
# field of an `mcp_servers` entry that way.
#
# MCP_INFERENCE_AUTH_TOKEN guards /mcp/inference (HttpMCPServerComponent~inference) - the
# task-scoped set for inferring a metamodel and publishing it to the model atlas. This is the
# endpoint event.atlas calls: the value must match METAMODEL_MCP_TOKEN in that repo's own
# secrets.bndrun, alongside a METAMODEL_MCP_URL pointing at this servlet's public tunnel.
#
# MCP_EMF_AUTH_TOKEN guards /mcp/emf (HttpMCPServerComponent~emfModel) - the full 38-tool
# surface. Give it its own value: rotating one endpoint should not disturb the other, and the
# two expose very different amounts of the runtime.
-runvm.secrets: \
	-DMCP_INFERENCE_AUTH_TOKEN=REPLACE-ME,\
	-DMCP_EMF_AUTH_TOKEN=REPLACE-ME
